<title>CHINA: Shanghai to offer only lead-free petrol from Oct.</title>
<headline>Shanghai to offer only lead-free petrol from Oct.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai's petrol stations will offer only lead-free petrol from October 1 as part of the city's efforts to clean-up and protect the environment, the official Xinhua news agency said.</p>
<p>Shanghai had 744,000 motor vehicles at the end of 1996, which used a total of 1.1 million tonnes of petrol, 99 percent of it containing lead, Xinhua said in a report late on Monday .</p>
<p>It cited vehicle exhaust fumes as a major source of pollutants in the city.</p>
<p>-- Shanghai Newsroom (8621) 6279-7004</p>
</text>
